# Pre-commit (repave)

Run from **repo root** before every commit that touches runtime code (not docs-only).

## Standard loop

```bash
make format && make quality && make test
```

Before opening a PR that touches **any Python** (`**/*.py`), also run **`make security`**
when the diff includes **`engine/`**; for **scripts-only** Python, run Ruff and Bandit
on the changed paths (see **repave-python** skill).

- **`make format`** — `ruff format` on `engine/src` and `engine/tests` (run Ruff on other `.py` paths manually)
- **`make quality`** — `ruff check`, `ruff format --check`, **`mypy src`**
- **`make test`** — full pytest + coverage threshold (75%)

While editing Python, **`make test-fast`** skips `@pytest.mark.slow` and coverage.

## When to add checks

| Change | Also run |
|--------|----------|
| Any **`*.py`** | Follow `.cursor/rules/python-standards.mdc` and `python-security.mdc` |
| `engine/` Python | **`make security`** (Bandit + pip-audit — same as CI) |
| `scripts/` or other `.py` | `cd engine && uv run ruff check/format` on changed paths; Bandit if security-relevant |
| `operator/` | **`make operator-lint`** and **`make operator-test`**; follow `golang-standards.mdc` / `golang-security.mdc` |
| `engine/pyproject.toml` deps | `make lock` and commit `engine/uv.lock` |
| Any **`*.js` / `*.mjs` / `*.cjs`** | **`make js-lint`**; follow `javascript-standards.mdc` / `javascript-security.mdc` |
| Helm chart | `make chart-validate` |

## Commits and PRs

- Conventional commits; PR titles validated by CI — see `.cursor/rules/pull-requests.mdc`.
- Ship **tests in the same PR** as new engine behavior unless the change is docs-only.

Details: `CONTRIBUTING.md`; Python: `.cursor/rules/python-standards.mdc`, security: `.cursor/rules/python-security.mdc`; JavaScript: `.cursor/rules/javascript-standards.mdc`, `.cursor/rules/javascript-security.mdc`; Go: `.cursor/rules/golang-standards.mdc`, `.cursor/rules/golang-security.mdc`.
